---
import DevLayout from '../../layouts/DevLayout.astro';
---

<DevLayout
  title="Data Model - Developer Guide - Salesdam"
  description="Database schemas and entity relationships"
>
  <h1>Data Model</h1>

  <p>
    This document describes the MongoDB database schemas, model relationships,
    and data structures used throughout Salesdam.
  </p>

  <h2>Entity Relationships</h2>

  <pre><code>Tenant (1) → (N) User
Tenant (1) → (N) ObjectMeta
Tenant (1) → (N) Session
Tenant (1) → (N) Role
Tenant (1) → (N) Automation
Tenant (1) → (N) Dashboard

ObjectMeta (1) → (N) FieldMeta
ObjectMeta (1) → (N) DynamicRecord

User (N) → (1) Role
User (N) → (1) Tenant

FieldMeta (lookup) → ObjectMeta (reference to other objects)</code></pre>

  <h2>Session Model Fields</h2>
  <pre><code>sessionId: String (unique, indexed)
userId: ObjectId → User
tenantId: ObjectId → Tenant
data: Map (session data)
expiresAt: Date (TTL indexed)
lastAccessedAt: Date
createdAt: Date
ipAddress: String
userAgent: String</code></pre>

  <h2>Key Models Summary</h2>

  <p>See the Architecture and Authentication pages for complete schema definitions.</p>

  <h3>Tenant</h3>
  <p>Workspace container. All data scoped to tenantId.</p>

  <h3>User</h3>
  <p>User accounts with email, password (hashed), roleId.</p>

  <h3>ObjectMeta</h3>
  <p>Custom object definitions (label, apiName, fields).</p>

  <h3>FieldMeta</h3>
  <p>Field definitions (type, required, unique, validation).</p>

  <h3>DynamicRecord</h3>
  <p>Flexible record storage with Map-based data field.</p>
</DevLayout>
